name: Bounded pack inspection, legacy draft consumption and deliberate scope review
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/pack_inspection.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
paste-file: @ART/limited-command.txt
keys: Enter
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 pack walk-entry limit reached | limited
expect: Incomplete inspection
expect: entries 1/1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/pack_inspection.py @TMP_TARGET @ART limited
ask: Does the result expose the finite walk allowance and omitted checks without claiming a clean pack or completed Map?
submit: run pack:suggest-shards {}
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 never auto-installed | draft
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/pack_inspection.py @TMP_TARGET @ART consume-draft
paste-file: @ART/complete-command.txt
keys: Enter
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 Inspection: complete=true | complete
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/pack_inspection.py @TMP_TARGET @ART complete
ask: Does exact compatibility dispatch produce a draft that the linter can consume while modern scope acceptance and scan work remain separate?
paste-file: @ART/oversized-command.txt
keys: Enter
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 reserved bytes 16/16 | oversized
expect: size of 16 bytes
expect: 1 error(s)
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/pack_inspection.py @TMP_TARGET @ART oversized
resize: 40x12
keys: Escape
wait: 0.2
keys: z
require-live-snap: 20 READ TRANSCRIPT | failed-reader-40x12
expect: Ctrl+G palette
expect-not: z expand
keys: PPage
live-snap: failed-reader-page-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: failed-reader-second-page-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: failed-reader-third-page-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: failed-reader-allowance-40x12
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/pack_inspection.py @TMP_TARGET @ART reader
keys: C-g
require-live-snap: 20 COMMAND PALETTE | reader-palette-40x12
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 READ TRANSCRIPT | reader-return-40x12
ask: Can the operator read the failed inspection and its retained allowance without hidden model work or unreadable narrow chrome?
resize: 120x36
keys: Escape
submit: scopes
require-live-snap: 20 Enter / c build inventory | empty-scopes
keys: c
require-live-snap: 30 DRAFT SCOPES | whole-scope
keys: z
require-live-snap: 20 DRAFT SCOPES | scope-keeps-input
keys: f
require-live-snap: 20 README.md | loose-root-file
ask: Does the modern whole-repository draft retain loose root files and show concrete membership before acceptance?
keys: Escape
resize: 160x48
live-snap: scope-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: scope-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: scope-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: scope-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 15 Enter menu | scope-40x12
expect: p plan
keys: NPage NPage
live-snap: scope-page-40x12
ask: Are scope, evidence and actions readable across all six sizes without allowing drafts or lint results to imply a scan plan?
keys: Escape
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
resize: 80x24
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: scopes
require-live-snap: 25 DRAFT SCOPES | no-color-scopes
expect-not: Map ✓
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/pack_inspection.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does restart retain the draft and inspection history without forging Map completion, spending or discovery work?
keys: Escape
wait: 0.2
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
